    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are locked and loaded for today\u2019s slate, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Yordan Alvarez** (81.62), who command the highest efficiency scores of the day. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a priority start, leveraging a prime leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Houck; his projected 85% stolen base success rate against a slow delivery makes him the foundational piece of our roster strategy today. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.443 xwOBA and a favorable platoon advantage against Johnson, setting him up for high-impact production in the two-hole. **Trea Turner** (72.06) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) also provide significant upside, though **Trea Turner** carries slight risk due to wind-in conditions that may suppress power ceilings, despite his elite leadoff projection.\n\nOur bench optimization was razor-thin today, with **Carson Benge** (54.74) falling just short of forcing a lineup change. While **Carson Benge** offered a solid profile against Herz, the collective efficiency of our starting outfield and the high-ceiling platoon edges for players like **Christian Yelich** (67.45)\u2014who gains a massive 13% boost from his dynamic platoon matchup against Pallante\u2014kept **Carson Benge** on the pine. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Junior Caminero** (54.45), whose score is suppressed by a tough matchup against the perennial ace Wheeler; however, his lineup placement and base skills keep him as a marginal start over alternatives like **Jacob Gonzalez** (43.19). With **Colt Keith** still sidelined on the IL, we are managing our remaining depth carefully to maximize our 5x5 category output as we approach the season's final days.",
